{"id":"27cacb208c303314","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-thm-perfect-set-cardinality-theorem.md","title":"Perfect Set Cardinality","display":"thm-perfect-set-cardinality-theorem — Perfect Set Cardinality","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-perfect-set-cardinality-theorem","aliases":["58-thm-perfect-set-cardinality-theorem","Perfect Set Cardinality","Cantor-Bendixson"],"display":"thm-perfect-set-cardinality-theorem — Perfect Set Cardinality","depends_on":["[[../batch08/58-df-perfect.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]]","[[58-df-cardinality.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-aleph.md]]","[[../batch09/58-df-cardinal-exponentiation.md]]","[[../batch14/58-df-cardinalexpp.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-perfect-set-cardinality-theorem"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-perfect-set-cardinality-theorem</span><span>Perfect Set Cardinality</span><span>Cantor-Bendixson</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-perfect-set-cardinality-theorem — Perfect Set Cardinality"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"f6afc84fe5b2b44e\" href=\"?note=f6afc84fe5b2b44e\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-perfect.md\">../batch08/58-df-perfect.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md\">../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"2be08d4ee8aa1590\" href=\"?note=2be08d4ee8aa1590\" title=\"58-df-cardinality.md\">58-df-cardinality.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"535817bf563314f5\" href=\"?note=535817bf563314f5\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-aleph.md\">../batch17/58-df-aleph.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"e9a96ab954b6013e\" href=\"?note=e9a96ab954b6013e\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-cardinal-exponentiation.md\">../batch09/58-df-cardinal-exponentiation.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"949691fe1747f59d\" href=\"?note=949691fe1747f59d\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-cardinalexpp.md\">../batch14/58-df-cardinalexpp.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\\subseteq\\mathbb R\">\\(P\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d_{\\mathbb R}:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\">\\(d_{\\mathbb R}:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\)</span> is the standard metric, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d_{\\mathbb R}(x,y)=|x-y|\">\\(d_{\\mathbb R}(x,y)=|x-y|\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\\)</span> is the metric-space predicate from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md\">../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Perfect}_S(P,\\mathbb R,d_{\\mathbb R})\">\\(\\mathrm{Perfect}_S(P,\\mathbb R,d_{\\mathbb R})\\)</span> is the exact three-argument predicate from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"f6afc84fe5b2b44e\" href=\"?note=f6afc84fe5b2b44e\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-perfect.md\">../batch08/58-df-perfect.md</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|P|\">\\(|P|\\)</span> is the cardinality of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\">\\(P\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CardExp}_S(2,\\aleph_0)\">\\(\\mathrm{CardExp}_S(2,\\aleph_0)\\)</span> is the continuum cardinal from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"e9a96ab954b6013e\" href=\"?note=e9a96ab954b6013e\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-cardinal-exponentiation.md\">../batch09/58-df-cardinal-exponentiation.md</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}perfect\\text{-}set\\text{-}cardinality\\text{-}theorem}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(\\mathbb R,d_{\\mathbb R})\\land\n\\forall x,y\\in\\mathbb R\\;(d_{\\mathbb R}(x,y)=|x-y|)\\land\nP\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\land\\mathrm{Perfect}_S(P,\\mathbb R,d_{\\mathbb R})\\land P\\neq\\emptyset\n\\to |P|=\\mathrm{CardExp}_S(2,\\aleph_0)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}perfect\\text{-}set\\text{-}cardinality\\text{-}theorem}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(\\mathbb R,d_{\\mathbb R})\\land\n\\forall x,y\\in\\mathbb R\\;(d_{\\mathbb R}(x,y)=|x-y|)\\land\nP\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\land\\mathrm{Perfect}_S(P,\\mathbb R,d_{\\mathbb R})\\land P\\neq\\emptyset\n\\to |P|=\\mathrm{CardExp}_S(2,\\aleph_0)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The exact three-argument perfect-set predicate is instantiated with the standard real metric; the cardinality, aleph, and cardinal-exponentiation operators all have direct dependencies.</li>\n<li>A nonempty perfect subset of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R\">\\(\\mathbb R\\)</span> has continuum cardinality.</li>\n<li>Cantor set: explicit example.</li>\n<li>Every closed subset of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{R}\">\\(\\mathbb{R}\\)</span> decomposes into a perfect part and a countable scattered part.</li>\n<li>Applications: descriptive set theory.</li>\n<li>PSP: perfect set property.</li>\n<li>Measure vs. size: Cantor set has measure zero but size continuum.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch08/58-df-perfect.md","status":"resolved","id":"f6afc84fe5b2b44e","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-df-perfect.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"ce876585d129ce97","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-cardinality.md","status":"resolved","id":"2be08d4ee8aa1590","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-cardinality.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-aleph.md","status":"resolved","id":"535817bf563314f5","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-aleph.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-cardinal-exponentiation.md","status":"resolved","id":"e9a96ab954b6013e","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-cardinal-exponentiation.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch14/58-df-cardinalexpp.md","status":"resolved","id":"949691fe1747f59d","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch14/58-df-cardinalexpp.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"ce876585d129ce97","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S$ is the metric-space predicate from [[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]].","embed":false},{"target":"../batch08/58-df-perfect.md","status":"resolved","id":"f6afc84fe5b2b44e","anchor":"ref-8","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Perfect}_S(P,\\mathbb R,d_{\\mathbb R})$ is the exact three-argument predicate from [[../batch08/58-df-perfect.md]].","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/5